TITLE:: RLVoiceLeading
summary:: How the voices of one chord move to the tones of the next, by the least motion
categories:: Libraries>reLation
related:: Classes/RLWalk, Classes/RLPitchSystem, Classes/RLChord, Guides/reLation

DESCRIPTION::
A strong::voicing:: is an Array of pitches of one link::Classes/RLPitchSystem::, one per voice, in the order of the voices (not sorted: voice 0 stays voice 0). link::#*minimal:: sends each voice to one tone of the target so that the total motion is least; each voice then takes the nearest pitch of its tone.

A least motion never needs crossed voices (Tymoczko, emphasis::The geometry of musical chords::, 2006), so it is one of the rotations of the two chords sorted round the pitch-class circle: n candidates for n voices, not n!. link::#*exhaustive:: tries every assignment and is there to check the first.

Sizes are in cents, so that motions in different systems compare.

code::
~edo = RLEDO(12);
RLVoiceLeading.minimal(~edo, [60, 64, 67], [0, 3, 7]);    // [60, 63, 67]: C major to C minor
RLVoiceLeading.minimal(~edo, [60, 64, 67], [5, 9, 0]);    // [60, 65, 69]: C major to F major
RLVoiceLeading.cents(~edo, [60, 64, 67], [60, 65, 69]);   // 300.0
RLVoiceLeading.displacements(~edo, [60, 64, 67], [60, 65, 69]);   // [0.0, 100.0, 200.0]

~just = RLJust([3, 5]);     // 1/1, 5/4, 3/2 to the tones 5/3, 1/1, 5/4
RLVoiceLeading.minimal(~just, [[0, 0, 0], [-2, 0, 1], [-1, 1, 0]], [[-1, 1], [0, 0], [0, 1]]);
// [[0, 0, 0], [-2, 0, 1], [0, -1, 1]]: the fifth moves up to 5/3, a minor tone 10/9 (182.4 cents)
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: minimal
The voicing of the target tones nearest to a voicing.
argument:: system
argument:: voices
The voicing to move from.
argument:: pcs
The target's pitch classes, as many as there are voices (double a tone by naming it twice).

METHOD:: exhaustive
The same by trying every assignment of voices to tones: for tests, and for chords of up to six voices.

METHOD:: displacements
How far each voice moves between two voicings, in cents, signed.

METHOD:: cents
The size of the motion between two voicings.
argument:: system
argument:: from
argument:: to
argument:: measure
code::\l1:: the sum of the moves (the default), code::\l2:: their Euclidean length, code::\linf:: the largest.

METHOD:: closePosition
A chord in close position: its tones in the order of its type's pattern, the root nearest a height, each next tone above the last.
argument:: chord
An link::Classes/RLChord::.
argument:: height
In octaves above the origin.
